      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Toast the walnuts and blind bake the pastry"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Spread the walnuts on a baking tray and toast at 180°C for 8 minutes until fragrant. Set aside. Make, chill, and blind bake the pastry case at 190°C with beans for 15 minutes, then without for 8 minutes until just cooked through. The case should not be too coloured, it will bake further with the filling."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Mix the filling and bake"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Reduce the oven to 170°C conventional (150°C fan). Whisk together the maple syrup, brown sugar, melted butter, beaten eggs, vanilla, and salt until combined. Spread the toasted walnuts in the pastry case. Pour the filling over the walnuts, they will float to the surface. Bake for 35 to 40 minutes until the filling is set with a firm jiggle across the whole tart (not a liquid wobble). Cool completely on a wire rack before cutting, at least 1 hour."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
